From f8d6fddf4ad9616224b44cf2d581dcd4aff38137 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: GNB Build <palimpseste@quidam.eu>
Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 19:18:01 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 17/17] feat(ui): add accent_cyan color, use it for BLE/WiFi
 on-state text

corp_blue is shared with the title bar, ADVERT icon, and the non-exclusive
Bluetooth icon page, so it can't be recolored for just the BLE/WiFi status
text without a global re-theme. Added a dedicated UIColor::accent_cyan
instead, defined per display driver mirroring corp_blue's pattern: a real
bright cyan on the color-capable TFT drivers (ST7735 [WT2], ST7789LCD,
NV3001B, LGFX), identical to the existing corp_blue value everywhere else
(monochrome OLED / e-ink), so nothing changes visually on those boards.

Applied to the EXCLUSIVE_BLE_WIFI on-state text on the BLUETOOTH and WIFI
home pages only (the requested scope): corp_blue's current dark navy
(0x001A) read as too dark on the WT2's screen when the active protocol
is shown 'on'. Off-state (secondary_txt, gray) untouched. The legacy
DUAL_BLE_WIFI WiFi page keeps corp_blue, out of scope for this request.
